479713?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott","html_url":"https://github.com/atscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-06-15T19:59:00Z","updated_at":"2020-06-15T19:59:00Z","body":"Yep, I actually ran into this 10 minutes ago myself. The issue is that new navigations cancel the previous one (via the `switchMap`) and the `finalize` stage of that cancelled navigation clears the `currentNavigation`:\r\nhttps://github.com/angular/angular/blob/cc49a91de7e228c6bdff8ca58936f05abe0ceb9f/packages/router/src/router.ts#L756\r\nAnd then the `finalUrl` part:\r\nhttps://github.com/angular/angular/blob/cc49a91de7e228c6bdff8ca58936f05abe0ceb9f/packages/router/src/router.ts#L506-L509\r\nA potential fix might be to only set `currentNavigation` to `null` if the cancelled transition's `navigationId` is equal to the one on `currentNavigation`. At first glance, this seems like the correct fix, but maybe I'm missing something - I'd like to assume there was a reason it wasn't written that way from the beginning.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/644347314/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commente